[Mission.Objectives]
Establish a springboard
[Mission.Description]
Major Gerhard, you must establish a springboard for an offensive on Sbeitla by destroying the enemy defences in this area. Crush the enemy with our tanks.
[Mission.Success]
We have prepared the springboard for the offensive. Enemy defences have been destroyed.
[Mission.Failed]
Retreat. We have failed to break the enemy resistance in this area.
[SubMission_01.Objectives]
Destroy enemy recon teams
[SubMission_01.Description]
We must destroy enemy recon teams as quickly as possible to prevent them from informing their high command about our strength and disposition.
[SubMission_01.Success]
Recon teams have been destroyed, enemy infantry is fleeing.
[SubMission_01.Failed]
[SubMission_02.Objectives]
Outflank the enemy
[SubMission_02.Description]
Our intelligence reports indicate that an artillery battery is defending the road. We must outflank the enemy main line of defence. Make use of the riverbed. I assume the enemy will fire at the valley. We must redeploy the troops to a safe place as soon as possible.
[SubMission_02.Success]
We have successfully outflanked the main body of the enemy.
[SubMission_02.Failed]
[SubMission_03.Objectives]
Establish radio communication
[SubMission_03.Description]
Our recon found a place for radio contact, but it's secured by the enemy. We must eliminate them and take one of our tanks or armoured vehicles to that location.
[SubMission_03.Success]
The enemy has been destroyed, the height is secured.
[SubMission_03.Failed]
[SubMission_04.Objectives]
Eliminate artillery battery
[SubMission_04.Description]
The enemy has redeployed an artillery battery on the island. We must eliminate it. 
[SubMission_04.Success]
The enemy artillery battery has been eliminated.
[SubMission_04.Failed]
[SubMission_05.Objectives]
Find a safe passage
[SubMission_05.Description]
Before the final offensive we must check the crossings for minefields.
[SubMission_05.Success]
A safe crossing has been found.
[SubMission_05.Failed]
[StringTable.Rommel_01]
I do count on you and your men, Major. I understand that the men are weary, but the situation demands that we mobilize our best qualities. Such days give rise to heroes to be remembered by generations to come.
[StringTable.Gerhard_01]
General, sir! There is no need to say this to me and my men. We are soldiers of the German Reich, and we always remember this! However, your presence here, on the front line, will help us forget the weariness and fight valiantly!
[StringTable.Gerhard_02]
Yes, general, sir! ...Damn! We've lost contact with high command. Mountains must be shielding our transmitters. We must re-establish contact as soon as possible.
[StringTable.Gerhard_03]
What's going on? Re-establish the radio contact immediately!